From f5fbcd63f0f0b184041e798b4a68fbf58c025c87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Kannegaard Hayes <philiphayes9@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:07:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] node: report readiness and phase to systemd (sd_notify)

Send `READY=1` once the datadir is locked, before the store opens, so a
`Type=notify` start job (boot, `systemctl restart`, a deploy) does not wait
out a schema migration or catch-up. Mirror each phase change into the
unit's status text and send `STOPPING=1` at shutdown.

std-only: one datagram to `$NOTIFY_SOCKET` (a path or a Linux `@abstract`
name). A no-op when unset and on non-Unix targets.
